            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ночью в школе зазвенел сигнал тревоги. Nóchyu v shkóle zazvenél signál trevógi. At night the alarm went off in the school."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also \"worry\": с тревогой — anxiously. Пожарная тревога (trevóga) — a fire alarm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "тревога (trevóga) is inherited from Proto-Slavic trĭvoga (EtymDB); its deeper origin is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
